      "summaryMarkdown": "REL-1: `dist-workspace.toml` carries every required key (dist 0.33.0, six targets, shell/powershell, sha256, install-updater false, github hosting, install-path `[$RAYX_HOME/bin, ~/.rayx/bin]`, attestations, pr-run-mode upload, windows-2022 custom runner with x86_64 host and no container, no allow-dirty). `release.yml` differs from the previous version only by dist's 0.33.0 output (version URL, attestation permissions and `actions/attest` step, rust-cache); tag trigger unchanged. `dist plan` (0.33.0) and `dist generate --check` succeed with a clean tree, and the plan matrix shows six hosted-runner entries, none with a container. The five tests in `tests/release_config.rs` assert the config and the generated workflow and pass. REL-2: Release run 38561390146 on draft PR #1 succeeded for all six build-local-artifacts jobs (aarch64-pc-windows-msvc on windows-2022, Attest step green) plus plan and build-global-artifacts. Re-extracted artifacts: all six `.sha256` match; aarch64 `rayx.exe` is PE32+ Aarch64, x86_64 one is x86-64; both musl binaries are static (static-pie / statically linked); macOS binaries are arm64 and x86_64 Mach-O; installers, sha256.sum and dist manifests are present. Both installers install to `$RAYX_HOME/bin` or `~/.rayx/bin` and write `rayx-cli-receipt.json` for app name `rayx-cli`, matching `APP_NAME` in `src/update.rs`. Rules and decision honoured: no hand edit, no allow-dirty, asset names unchanged, hosted runners only.",
